This repository provides a downstream SuperMimic implementation for UniLab.
UniLab and UniSim are separate upstream projects licensed under Apache-2.0.

The implementation was developed with reference to the SuperMimic reference
code in supermimic_vibed, whose MIT license and original copyright notice are
preserved in LICENSES/MIT-supermimic.txt.

SuperMimic paper:
"SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control with One Differentiable
World Model", Qiayuan Liao et al., https://supermimic.github.io

th_supermimic adaptations:
- K1/G1 per-run robot specifications, dimension-generic MDP and context layouts.
- RIMKit model preparation, RMAI named-joint import and portable training launcher.
- K1 PD gains/default positions/action scales reference the local th_beyondmimic
  K1 configuration. Robot assets are generated from RIMKit and retain vendor
  license/attribution files. They are excluded from the source archive.
- SuperMimic-Reproduced was inspected as an independent reference; its reported
  benchmark results are not results of this repository.

Standalone runtime revision:
- UniLab/UniSim/mjlab runtime dependencies removed. Direct MuJoCo and MuJoCo
  Warp backends, collector/reset lifecycle, CLI, and checkpoint identity guards
  are implemented inside th_supermimic.
- Retained algorithm/math modules preserve their original attribution above.
